From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: OSI: hide Windows 2022 from the Lenovo Yoga 9 2-in-1 16N1X11

The Yoga 9 2-in-1 16N1X11 (83N7, NVIDIA N1x) hides \_SB.SSPM (NVDA8400)
from an OS that claims Windows 2022, like the Lenovo Pro 9 15N1X11, so
the keyboard, touchpad, audio, USB4 and EC never power on. Tested with
acpi_osi="!Windows 2022" on the command line.

---
 drivers/acpi/osi.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/acpi/osi.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/osi.c
@@ -488,6 +488,14 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id acpi_osi_dmi_table[] __initconst = {
 		    DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "83SS"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+	.callback = dmi_disable_osi_win11_22h2,
+	.ident = "Lenovo Yoga 9 2-in-1 16N1X11",
+	.matches = {
+		    DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "LENOVO"),
+		    DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "83N7"),
+		},
+	},
 	/*
 	 * ASUS's \MSOS tries "Windows 2022" and then "Windows 2001", so
 	 * without the first it reports Windows XP, and the EC event handler
